      "text": "To find the length of the hypotenuse \\( h \\) of a right triangle with legs \\( \\log_4 27 \\) and \\( \\log_2 9 \\), we first need to simplify these logarithmic expressions.\n\n1. Simplify \\( \\log_4 27 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\log_4 27 = \\log_{4} (3^3) = \\frac{\\log_2 27}{\\log_2 4} = \\frac{\\log_2 3^3}{\\log_2 2^2} = \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\log_4 27 = \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify \\( \\log_2 9 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\log_2 9 = \\log_2 (3^2) = 2 \\log_2 3\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\log_2 9 = 2 \\log_2 3\n   \\]\n\n3. Use the Pythagorean theorem to find \\( h \\):\n   \\[\n   h = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2} \\right)^2 + (2 \\log_2 3)^2}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n   \\[\n   h = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2} \\right)^2 + (2 \\log_2 3)^2} = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2} \\right)^2 + (2 \\log_2 3)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9 (\\log_2 3)^2}{4} + 4 (\\log_2 3)^2}\n   \\]\n   Combine the terms under the square root:\n   \\[\n   h = \\sqrt{\\frac{9 (\\log_2 3)^2 + 16 (\\log_2 3)^2}{4}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25 (\\log_2 3)^2}{4}} = \\frac{5 \\log_2 3}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. Compute \\( 4^h \\):\n   \\[\n   4^h = 4^{\\frac{5 \\log_2 3}{2}} = (2^2)^{\\frac{5 \\log_2 3}{2}} = 2^{5 \\log_2 3} = (2^{\\log_2 3})^5 = 3^5 = 243\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( 4^h \\) is \\(\\boxed{243}\\).",
